<Control id="BTN-COLLECT" type="Button" x="868" y="192" w="200" h="40" tab-order="11" z-order="11" visible="true" enabled="true" parent="CARD-IN">
    <Property name="Caption">Coletar do veículo</Property>
    <Property name="FontSize">14</Property>
    <Property name="Bold">true</Property>
    <Property name="CornerRadius">10</Property>
    <Property name="TextAlignment">MiddleCenter</Property>
    <Property name="BackgroundColor">#5B4FE9FF</Property>
    <Property name="ForegroundColor">#FFFFFFFF</Property>
    <Property name="BorderStyle">None</Property>
    <Property name="Anchor">Top,Left</Property>
    <Property name="Definition">Collects the readings of the connected vehicle (simulated) and saves the diagnosis.</Property>
    <Event name="onClick" paragraph="BTN-COLLECT--ONCLICK"><![CDATA[       ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.

       DATA DIVISION.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
           *> DIAG-COLLECT: collects the vehicle (mode S) and saves the diagnosis.
           *> Uses:   DCQ-PLATE = TXT-PLATE; DCQ-MODE = "S"; DCQ-ID = 0 (a new collection);
           *>         DCQ-INTERRUPT-AFTER = the sensor typed in TXT-DROP when CHK-DROP is ticked, else 0.
           *> Result: DCS-STATUS = OK, PARTIAL, NOVEHICLE, INVALID or ERROR; with OK or PARTIAL the
           *>         readings and fault codes (DCS-...) are shown below and DCS-ID is kept in WS-DIAG-ID.

           INITIALIZE    DGC-REQ
           SET     DCQ-PLATE                     TO    TXT-PLATE::Text
           SET     DCQ-OPERATOR                  TO    TXT-OPERATOR::Text
           SET     DCQ-MODE                      TO    "S"
           IF    CHK-DROP::Checked = 1
               COMPUTE DCQ-INTERRUPT-AFTER       =     FUNCTION NUMVAL ( TXT-DROP::Text )
           END-IF

           SET     DCS-STATUS                    TO    SPACES
           CALL    "DIAG-COLLECT" WITH WEBSOCKET LINKAGE
               USING BY VALUE DGC-REQ
               RETURNING DGC-RES
               ON EXCEPTION
                   COBOL::"WS-LAST-ERROR" ( BE-CLASS BE-CODE BE-MSG )
                   SET     DCS-STATUS            TO    "CALL"
           END-CALL

           *> SHOW-RESULT: paints the answer of DIAG-COLLECT on the result card and the status line.
           *> Uses:   DCS-... = the answer just received; DCS-STATUS decides what is shown.
           *> Result: LBL-V-... captions and LBL-STATUS::Caption are set; WS-DIAG-ID keeps the number of
           *>         a partial collection (0 otherwise) so the manual entry can complete it.

           CALL    "SHOW-RESULT"
]]></Event>
  </Control>
